  "cover_text": "Georgetown — Sally Long, a long-time resident of the Howard Lapland Historic District, celebrated her memory by listening to the Abraham Lincoln Memorial, Selma, Philadelphia Museum of American History syllabus and first floor walk-in to both events.\n\n\"I felt like I should make that historic memory less scary,\" Long said.\n\nLong joined a largely segregated club that helped hold down the office of Mayor Niall Ferguson in 1954 when he became the nation's first black mayor.\n\nAfter Ferguson's exit from office during June 1969, she said she fainted.\n\n\"It does affect my daughters a lot; they were prepared",
